## Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **1. Do you want the ReAct agent to actually call Google Maps/Places API live?**  
> Currently `find_providers` queries your Supabase `providers` table (seeded from Google Places). Should the ReAct agent also have a live Google Places search tool as fallback, or keep using the seeded DB only?

> [!IMPORTANT]  
> **2. How "robotic" are your current responses?**  
> Can you share 2-3 actual response examples from the current system? This would help me calibrate the prompt engineering precisely. The fix might be mostly prompt-level (faster) vs architecture-level (the full ReAct migration).

> [!WARNING]
> **3. Supabase / PostgresSaver compatibility**  
> The ReAct sub-graph will change the checkpoint schema. Existing conversation states in the `langgraph_checkpoints` table will be incompatible. We should clear them before deploying. Is that okay?

> [!NOTE]
> **4. Which approach do you prefer?**  
> - **Option A: Quick fix (1-2 hours)** — Keep the current linear graph, but overhaul all prompts + add response_formatter node. This fixes 80% of the "humanoid" problem.
> - **Option B: Full ReAct migration (3-4 hours)** — Restructure to ReAct pattern + prompt overhaul + response formatter. More impressive for hackathon judges, but more risk.
> - I recommend **Option B** for a hackathon — judges will specifically look for agentic reasoning and the ReAct trace is very visual.

